<title>USA: Intl Paper unit buys Finland's Forchem.</title>
<headline>Intl Paper unit buys Finland's Forchem.</headline>
<dateline>PANAMA CITY, Fla. 1996-08-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Arizona Chemical said Friday it acquired Forchem, a tall oil and turpentine processor in Finland, for undisclosed terms.</p>
<p>Forchem was purchased from Enso-Gutzeit Oy and UPM Kymmene, two Finnish forest and paper products companies. Arizona Chemical is the specialty products business of International Paper Co.</p>
<p>In 1995, it said, Forchem's sales were $92 million.</p>
<p>The acquisition involves two manufacturing locations, one in Oulu, Finland, and the other in Valkeakoski, Finland.</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk 212-859-1610.</p>
</text>
